---
// Privacy copy must match the optional voice demo, external media, and SMS form.
//
// Do NOT replace this with a boilerplate policy pulled from another company.
// A borrowed Terms/Privacy pair belonging to "Uppit AI LLC" was considered for
// this page and rejected: it was someone else's copyrighted text, and it
// described SMS opt-in flows, form fields including budget range, cookies,
// pixels and analytics vendors. A privacy policy is
// a legal representation. Claiming to collect data you do not collect is its
// own kind of false statement.
//
// UPDATED 2026-08-21: the site gained its first form -- the SMS opt-in at
// /text-me -- and this file changed in the same commit, as the note below
// required. The "no contact forms" claim was removed because it became false.
//
// If the site adds another data-collecting feature, update this file in the
// same change. The SMS section is also a carrier compliance
// artefact: the 10DLC campaign cites this policy, and carriers require that it
// forbid sharing opt-in data with third parties. Do not weaken that paragraph.
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { contact } from '../data/site.js';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  kicker="What the website, sample demo, and text request collect."
  updated="October 21, 2026"
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    Client Optimal does not currently use first-party analytics. The recorded
    sample is hosted by YouTube, and the optional browser voice demo connects to
    a third-party voice AI provider. Those services may receive technical information when their
    features load or run. We do not sell or rent personal information.
  </p>
  <p>
    The optional <a href="/text-me">text me the demo</a> form collects
    information for the requested sample and SMS consent. The browser sample
    requests microphone access only when you choose to start it.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <p>
    Website hosting and domain providers may record technical request
    information such as IP address, browser type, and requested page. YouTube
    and our voice AI provider are third-party providers used only when their media or voice
    demo features load or run.
  </p>
  <p>
    The interactive sample sends browser microphone audio to our voice AI
    provider over a WebRTC connection. A transcript may be displayed in the browser. The sample
    does not place a phone call, send a text, create a booking, or handle a real
    customer request. Do not provide real phone numbers, addresses, payment
    details, or sensitive information.
  </p>
  <p>
    The voice AI provider's current terms describe call recording and
    processing for analytics and service improvement when recording has not
    been disabled.
    Client Optimal has not verified the account's recording, transcription,
    retention, or model-use settings, or the resulting retention period. These
    settings must be confirmed before the demo is treated as approved for real
    information or before a client call flow goes live. To ask which provider
    is used or how its settings are configured, email us at the address on the
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Text messages, and what we do with your number</h2>
  <p>
    If you submit the form on the <a href="/text-me">text me the demo</a> page,
    you are giving us express written consent to send you text messages about
    the demo you asked for and follow-up about that service.
    <strong>Message frequency may vary.</strong>
    <strong>Standard message and data rates may apply.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Consent to receive text messages is <strong>not a condition of any
    purchase</strong>. The checkbox is never pre-ticked, and SMS consent is
    asked for separately from anything else.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>To stop receiving messages, reply STOP to any message.</strong> That
    removes your number permanently and automatically, and we check that
    suppression list at the moment of sending rather than when a batch is built,
    so an opt-out always takes effect. Reply <strong>HELP</strong> for help, or
    email <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you submit the form we record your name, business name, phone number,
    the date and time, your IP address, and the exact version of the consent
    wording shown to you. We keep that record so we can demonstrate, if a
    carrier or regulator ever asks, that you agreed and what you agreed to.
  </p>
  <h2>Your mobile information is never sold or shared</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Your mobile information will not be sold or shared with third
    parties for promotional or marketing purposes.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Mobile information will not be shared with third parties or
    affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.</strong> This covers
    sharing as well as selling, including any transfer to an affiliated or
    related business, whether or not money changes hands.
  </p>
  <p>
    Wherever this policy describes information being handled or disclosed:{' '}
    <strong>all the above categories exclude text messaging originator opt-in
    data and consent; this information will not be shared with any third
    parties.</strong> We will not share your opt-in to an SMS campaign with any
    third party for purposes unrelated to providing you with the services of
    that campaign.
  </p>
  <p>
    The one and only exception is delivery itself. Messages are transmitted by
    our telephony provider acting on our behalf, and they are not permitted to
    use your number for anything other than delivering the message you asked
    for. There is no advertising network, no data broker, and no affiliate
    involved at any point.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Consent records are kept for as long as we may need to demonstrate that you
    agreed, and are deleted on request.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Opt-outs are kept permanently, and that is deliberate.</strong> When
    you reply STOP, your number goes onto a suppression list that every send is
    checked against. That list is the only thing standing between you and being
    texted again, so deleting it would undo the very thing you asked for. It
    holds your number and nothing else: no name, no message history, no
    other detail.
  </p>

  <h2>If you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    Contact happens through LinkedIn or email. If you message us, we receive
    whatever you choose to send: your name, your email address, and whatever
    you write. We use it to reply to you and to discuss potential work. Nothing
    more.
  </p>
  <p>
    Those conversations sit on LinkedIn's and your email provider's systems, and
    their privacy policies apply to them, not ours.
  </p>

  <h2>The Client Optimal LinkedIn application</h2>
  <p>
    Client Optimal operates a private LinkedIn application used to publish posts
    to <strong>its own founder's LinkedIn account</strong>. It signs in through
    LinkedIn OAuth, which gives it that account's own profile identifier and
    permission to post as that account. It uses them for nothing else.
  </p>
  <p>
    The application <strong>does not read, collect, or store data about any other
    LinkedIn member</strong>. It does not access your profile, your connections,
    your feed, or your activity. It does not scrape LinkedIn, and it takes no
    automated action on anyone else's posts. It is private to Client Optimal and
    is not offered to anyone else.
  </p>
  <p>
    Running it involves a small number of service providers: the access token and
    the queued posts are held in the automation platform that runs the workflow,
    the drafts are generated by an AI provider, and approvals are sent through a
    messaging service. They process that information only to operate the
    workflow, on our instructions. None of it is sold, rented, or used for
    advertising, and none of it concerns visitors to this website.
  </p>
  <p>
    Separately, we sometimes write a reply to someone's public post by hand. Where
    we use our own tools to help draft one, the post is something we supplied
    manually, it is used only to prepare that reply, and we do not build or keep a
    profile of the person who wrote it. The reply is always reviewed and posted by
    a person.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell, rent, or trade personal information. We do not share it for
    anyone else's marketing purposes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Providers involved in this website include hosting and domain infrastructure,
    YouTube for the recorded sample, a voice AI provider for the optional
    browser voice demo, and the messaging/consent providers used if you request the demo by
    text. Their own privacy terms and retention settings also apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep correspondence for as long as it is useful to the conversation or
    the working relationship, and delete it when it is not. Hosting logs are
    retained by the hosting provider under its own schedule. The retention
    settings for the voice AI provider's audio and transcript data have not
    been verified;
    check the provider settings and terms before using the demo with real details.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    If you have emailed or messaged us and want that correspondence deleted,
    ask and we will delete it. For third-party demo data, contact the provider
    directly where applicable; Client Optimal must verify what data the provider
    retains and whether it can be deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is for business audiences and is not directed at children
    under 13. We do not knowingly collect information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This page should be updated when the demo provider, audio settings, SMS
    workflow, or data handling changes. Confirm the effective date and provider settings before publication.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can go to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>{' '}
    or via <a href={contact.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
